# Kept out of the distributed archive.
#
# Entries are exact relative file paths -- modkit matches them literally, so
# a bare "tests/" silently does nothing. Add the file, not the directory.

# The suite requires engine modules (tests.modkit, src.core.Data), which is a
# private require against the shipped package, and `pack` treats warnings as
# fatal.
tests/rby_mmo_test.lua

# The end-to-end drivers reach engine test infrastructure
# (tests/drivers/util.lua) and only mean anything inside a checkout.
tests/drivers/mmo_util.lua
tests/drivers/mmo_host.lua
tests/drivers/mmo_join.lua
tests/drivers/run-mmo-e2e.sh

# Working notes for whoever picks this up next; not mod content. The two
# machine-readable ones describe how coding agents are driven in this
# checkout -- they configure a tool, not a game, and a player who unpacks the
# archive has no use for either.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS_CONFIG.yml
skills-lock.json

# server/ is deliberately NOT ignored: hub.js is plain node with no engine
# imports, and someone who installs the package should be able to host.
#
# That reasoning now covers more files, and it still holds for all of them.
# server/bin/, server/lib/, server/package.json, server/Dockerfile and
# server/compose.yml stay in the archive for exactly the reason hub.js does:
# the person who unpacks this should be able to host a world without going
# back to GitHub for the missing half. `docker compose up` is only a complete
# answer if the compose file, the Dockerfile it builds and the package.json
# they describe all travel together -- ignoring any one of them would ship a
# compose file that cannot build. They are inert to the game client, which
# never opens anything under server/, and they carry no ROM-derived bytes, so
# neither `lint` nor the fatal-warning `pack` gate has anything to say about
# them.
#
# server/.dockerignore needs no entry and must not get one: modkit skips every
# dot-prefixed file when it walks the tree (tools/modkit.py:174-176), so it
# cannot be packed in the first place. The same is true of the .env and
# .github entries below, which are kept only as documentation of intent.
#
# server/hub.test.js is likewise left shipping, unchanged from before: it is
# self-contained node that drives the hub over real sockets, so it is a way a
# host can check their own copy works. It requires nothing from the engine,
# which is what earns `tests/rby_mmo_test.lua` its entry above and not this.

# tools/play.sh and tools/env.sh assume the engine checkout layout, and
# .env is machine-specific -- neither belongs in a distributed archive.
tools/env.sh
tools/play.sh
.env
.env.example

# Repo furniture, not mod content: the release pipeline and its notes.
# Implementation plans are working notes for contributors, on the same footing
# as CLAUDE.md above; each new one belongs on this list by name, because a
# bare docs/plans/ line would do nothing.
.github/workflows/release.yml
docs/plans/in-game-hosting.md
docs/plans/self-hosting-server-app.md

# Screenshots of a running game are composited from tiles, sprites and font
# glyphs decoded from the player's own ROM. They illustrate a GitHub page
# nobody installs; they are not bytes this project puts in an archive it
# hands out. modkit lint does not catch them -- MK302 compares a mod's PNGs
# against individual cache images, and a whole composited frame matches none
# of them -- so keeping them out is this file's job, not the linter's.
docs/screenshots/character-creation.png
docs/screenshots/character-picker.png
docs/screenshots/room-size.png
docs/screenshots/mmo-menu.png
docs/screenshots/overworld-presence.png
docs/screenshots/chat-log.png
docs/screenshots/interact-menu.png
docs/screenshots/link-battle.png
docs/screenshots/trainer-card.png
